---
import '../styles/studio.css';
import '../styles/asset-views.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="description" content="Create consistent orthographic asset views from one local GLB model, with pixel and voxel exports."/><title>3D Asset Views — Atelier</title></head><body>
<header><a class="brand" href="/studio/" aria-label="Atelier home"><span class="brand-mark">a.</span> atelier<span class="local">LOCAL</span></a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="/studio/">AI concepts</a><a href="#asset-form">3D Asset Views</a><a href="#asset-guide">How it works</a></nav><span id="health" role="status">Connecting …</span></header>
<main><section class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">ONE MODEL · EVERY DIRECTION</p><h1>Views that <span>belong together.</span></h1><p>Characters, karts, buildings and props. Seven cameras. One shared geometry.</p></div></section>
<div id="message" role="alert" hidden></div>
<section class="workspace" aria-label="Render asset views"><form id="asset-form" class="controls">
<div class="section-title"><h2>Import a model</h2><span>LOCAL · CPU</span></div>
<p class="hint">Start with your own GLB or try the original demo kart. All images render the same static pose.</p>
<label for="asset-file">Model · GLB file</label><input id="asset-file" type="file" accept=".glb,model/gltf-binary" aria-describedby="file-help file-state"/>
<p id="file-help" class="hint">Up to 32 MiB. Export glTF 2.0 Binary with embedded textures from Blender. Uncompressed meshes and PNG/JPEG textures.</p><p id="file-state" class="hint" role="status">No model selected.</p>
<button id="demo" class="quiet" type="button">Use demo kart</button>
<label for="asset-name">Asset name</label><input id="asset-name" maxlength="80" value="My asset" required/>
<label for="asset-style">Appearance</label><select id="asset-style"><option value="model">Original materials</option><option value="lowpoly">Low Poly · flat shading</option><option value="pixel">Pixel Art · shared palette</option><option value="voxel">Voxel Art · shared cube mesh</option></select>
<label for="asset-front">Front of the model · Blender coordinates</label><select id="asset-front" aria-describedby="axis-help"><option value="-Y">−Y · default</option><option value="+Y">+Y</option><option value="-X">−X</option><option value="+X">+X</option></select><p id="axis-help" class="hint">Z is up. Choose the axis pointing out of the nose or face. The top view puts this direction at the top of the image.</p>
<fieldset id="pixel-options" hidden><legend>Pixel export</legend><label for="asset-grid">Native grid</label><select id="asset-grid"><option value="32">32 × 32</option><option value="64">64 × 64</option><option value="128" selected>128 × 128</option></select><p class="hint">One palette for all seven views, no dithering, transparent background. Preview pixels are enlarged without smoothing.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset id="voxel-options" hidden><legend>Voxel conversion</legend><label for="voxel-grid">Cubes along the longest dimension</label><select id="voxel-grid"><option value="16">16 · chunky</option><option value="24" selected>24</option><option value="32">32</option><option value="48">48</option><option value="64">64 · finer</option></select><p class="hint">A surface approximation built once from the source. Thin details and gaps can change at this grid size. The download includes the derived cube mesh.</p></fieldset>
<div id="palette-options" hidden><label for="asset-colors">Maximum palette colors</label><select id="asset-colors"><option value="16">16</option><option value="24">24</option><option value="32" selected>32</option><option value="64">64</option><option value="128">128</option></select></div>
<p id="appearance-help" class="hint">Original materials preserve imported PBR. Flat shading changes normals and neutralizes gloss and emission; it does not reduce the polygon count.</p>
<button id="render-asset" class="primary" type="submit" disabled>Render seven views <span>↗</span></button><p class="save-note">Blender runs separately on the CPU. Your GPU image jobs can continue.</p>
</form><div class="visual"><div class="section-title"><h2>Shared model views</h2><span id="asset-status" role="status">READY WHEN YOU ARE</span></div><progress id="asset-progress" max="1" value="0" aria-label="Completed views" hidden></progress><button id="cancel-asset" class="quiet" type="button" hidden>Cancel render</button>
<div id="asset-empty" class="empty"><h3>Choose a model to begin.</h3><p>Front, left, right, back, top, bottom and three-quarter.<br/>Orthographic cameras with one shared scale and framing.</p></div>
<section id="asset-result" aria-label="Rendered asset" hidden><h3 id="result-name"></h3><img id="asset-sheet" alt="Contact sheet of all seven views from the same model"/><div id="asset-downloads" class="asset-downloads"></div><p id="asset-provenance" class="hint"></p><div id="asset-frames" class="asset-frames"></div></section>
<section class="queue" aria-labelledby="recent-title"><div class="section-title"><h2 id="recent-title">Recent model renders</h2><button id="refresh-assets" class="quiet" type="button">Refresh</button></div><div id="asset-jobs"><p class="hint">No model renders yet.</p></div></section></div></section>
<section id="asset-guide" class="guide"><div><p class="eyebrow">TWO WAYS TO BUILD ASSETS</p><h2>Explore the design.<br/>Then verify the model.</h2><p>The source model determines the real shape. These views preserve its geometry across cameras; they cannot certify anatomy, wheel count or mechanical correctness.</p></div><div><h3>1. AI concept presets</h3><p>Use Low Poly, Pixel Art or Voxel Art to explore a character, kart or prop. Concept sheets request four views in one image. AI can still change details, miss a direction or repeat a view.</p><div class="blender-starters"><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=lowpoly-kart-sheet">Low Poly sheet</a><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=pixel-character-sheet">Pixel sheet</a><a class="quiet" href="/studio/?recipe=voxel-prop">Voxel concept</a></div><h3>2. Build or import one model</h3><p>Model the selected concept in Blender, or import an existing asset. Export one self-contained GLB. Animated models use their imported pose at frame 1; animations, cameras and source lights are not exported with these views.</p></div><div><h3>3. Render and download</h3><p>The ZIP includes seven transparent PNGs, a contact sheet, the rendered GLB and a manifest with camera settings, dimensions and file hashes. Pixel exports also include native grid PNGs. All views share an orthographic scale.</p><h3>Color and voxel limits</h3><p>Pixel export quantizes the rendered light and material colors. Voxel conversion samples surface base colors, including basic image textures and vertex colors; complex shader effects are approximated. Review small features at your chosen resolution.</p><p>Imports stay in the local asset archive. They are separate from your AI image library. The original GLB is retained without modification.</p></div></section>
</main><footer><span>atelier / local asset studio</span><a href="/studio/">Back to image creation ↗</a></footer>
<dialog id="auth" aria-labelledby="auth-title"><form id="auth-form"><h2 id="auth-title">Connect to the service</h2><p>The API key is kept only in this tab’s memory.</p><label for="key">API key</label><input id="key" type="password" autocomplete="off" required/><button class="primary" type="submit">Connect</button></form></dialog>
<script>import '../scripts/asset-views.js';</script></body></html>
